1.27.2: HEIC told by content and converted on the way in; docs

- a HEIC/HEIF/AVIF is recognized by its ftyp box whatever the extension
  (a HEIC renamed .jpg included) and refused with the ways in: convert
  it, shoot JPEG or ProRAW, or install a converter. Native, wasm, and
  the page's drop zone (which checks the bytes before the engine sees
  them).
- the CLI (apply, develop, inspect) and 'polajuice serve' convert a
  HEIC themselves when heif-convert, heif-dec, magick, convert or sips
  is on the PATH: once, to NAME_from_heic.jpg beside the source, reused
  while it is newer than the source. The served strip lists HEICs
  (shown through the converter like a raw's straight print), renders
  and exports them, and keeps the derived JPEG out of the strip and the
  batch. EXIF orientation survives the round trip (checked with
  libheif's x265 build).
- src/cli/heic.c: fork/exec, no shell; linked into the CLIs only.

Tests: core (sniffing, refusal by content), compat and serve (a stub
HEIC and a stand-in converter on the PATH prove the plumbing without
libheif: conversion, reuse, derived file hidden, batch covers it),
wasm and page (refusal by content).

Docs: --help names HEIC and the converter; README title without a stale
version, HEIC section, completions in the install notes; ROADMAP marks
HEIC done as far as it goes (Display P3 still read as sRGB).
